---
// <GnnEdgeFigure> — one event through the edge classifier, on the neutrino page.
//
// Three panels: the raw hits on one wire plane, the kNN-8 cluster graph coloured
// by the network's merge probability, and the same graph carrying the truth
// labels. Read left to right it is the whole task: hits become Pandora cluster
// fragments, fragments become candidate edges, and the network decides which
// edges join fragments of the same particle.
//
// EVERY WORD IS STRIPPED. The source render carried a title, axis labels, tick
// labels, colourbars and two legends; all of it was cropped to the plot
// interiors and the legend boxes, which are opaque and hide nothing, painted
// out. That is what lets the figure sit on the page rather than on a white
// plate: with no type in it, there is nothing that has to stay dark to be read.
// The caption below carries what the labels used to say.
//
// Two variants, swapped on the theme. Both have the white ground removed by
// un-premultiplying, so the ink sits directly on the island. The dark variant
// lifts ONLY the near-black cluster nodes to pale; inverting every neutral pixel
// also inverted the colourmap's own pale centre, and the uncertain edges, which
// are the interesting ones, disappeared against the page.
//
// Source: MicroBooNE open data, v5 test event 273, CC νe, from the group's
// gnn_merge study. Delete the component and the page simply loses the figure.
const ALT =
  "Three panels for one simulated neutrino event. Left: the raw hits on one wire " +
  "plane, coloured by charge. Centre: the cluster graph, with every candidate edge " +
  "coloured by the network's merge probability, blue for low and red for high. " +
  "Right: the same graph with the true labels, red where an edge joins fragments of " +
  "the same particle and blue where it does not.";
---

<figure class="gnn">
  <img class="gnn-img gnn-img--light" src="/images/neutrino/gnn-edge-scores.png"
       alt={ALT} width="1450" height="601" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
  <img class="gnn-img gnn-img--dark" src="/images/neutrino/gnn-edge-scores-dark.png"
       alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1450" height="601" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
  <figcaption class="gnn-caption">
    One event through the edge classifier. Left, 791 raw hits on a single wire
    plane. Centre, the same hits grouped into cluster fragments and joined to
    their nearest neighbours, with each of the 910 candidate edges coloured by
    the network's merge probability, blue for low and red for high. Right, the
    truth: 601 edges join fragments of one particle, 309 join different ones. On
    this view the network reaches an edge F1 of 0.91.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gnn {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    /* Three wide panels: below this the detail stops being readable. */
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .gnn-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    min-width: 460px;
  }
  /* One variant per theme. The site sets data-theme explicitly, so this follows
     the toggle rather than the operating system. */
  .gnn-img--dark { display: none; }
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .gnn-img--light { display: none; }
  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .gnn-img--dark { display: block; }

  .gnn-caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
